 "standard_url": "https://www.cbseacademic.nic.in/web_material/CurriculumMain26/SrSec/Maths_SrSec_2025-26.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Derivative introduced as rate of change both as that of distance function and geometrically; intuitive idea of limit; limits of polynomials and rational functions, trigonometric, exponential and logarithmic functions; definition of derivative, relate it to slope of tangent of a curve; derivative of sum, difference, product and quotient of functions; derivatives of polynomial and trigonometric functions (summary of the CBSE syllabus)",
 "meta_desc": "Class 11 Limits and Derivatives worksheet (NCERT Chapter 12): limits by substitution and factorising, standard limits, sin x/x, derivatives of polynomials and trigonometric functions, product and quotient rules and first principles. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "lim (xⁿ − aⁿ)/(x − a) = naⁿ⁻¹ and lim sin x/x = 1.",
 "key_sub": "d/dx(xⁿ) = nxⁿ⁻¹; (uv)′ = u′v + uv′.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><ul><li>If substituting gives a number, that is the limit. If it gives 0/0, factorise and cancel first.</li><li>Standard limits: lim<sub>x→a</sub> (xⁿ − aⁿ)/(x − a) = naⁿ⁻¹; lim<sub>x→0</sub> sin x/x = 1.</li><li>Derivative: f′(x) = lim<sub>h→0</sub> [f(x + h) − f(x)]/h. d/dx(xⁿ) = nxⁿ⁻¹, d/dx(sin x) = cos x, d/dx(cos x) = −sin x.</li><li>Product rule (uv)′ = u′v + uv′; quotient rule (u/v)′ = (u′v − uv′)/v².</li></ul><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Evaluate lim<sub>x→2</sub> (x² − 4)/(x − 2).</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>0/0, so factorise: (x − 2)(x + 2)/(x − 2)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>= x + 2 → 4</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 4</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Stopping at 0/0 and saying the limit does not exist.</li><li>Writing d/dx(cos x) = sin x.</li><li>Using (uv)′ = u′v′.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "Is lim sin x/x = 1 true for x in degrees?",
   "a": "No. It needs x in radians."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the derivative of a constant?",
   "a": "0."
  }
